---
description: "Automated skills that run in response to agent actions"
globs: "**/*"
alwaysApply: true
---

## Skill: open-modified-buffers

After making file edits (via any tool that creates or modifies files), run the following command with every file that was modified or created:

```
~/.cursor/skills/open-modified-buffers.sh <file1> [file2] [file3] ...
```

This adds the modified files as buffers in the user's running neovim instance and triggers `checktime` so they reload automatically. Run this once at the end of a batch of edits, passing all changed file paths as arguments. Do not run it per-file individually.

## Skill: inject-todo-comment

When a build or test command fails, parse the error output for file paths and line numbers. For each distinct error location, run:

```
~/.cursor/skills/inject-todo-comment.sh <keyword> <file> <line> <message>
```

- Use `FIX` as the keyword for build/compile errors.
- Use `FAILED` as the keyword for test failures.
- `<message>` should be a concise summary of the error, not the raw compiler dump.
- After injecting comments, run the open-modified-buffers skill on every file that received a comment so the user sees them immediately.
- Do not inject duplicate comments if the same error at the same location has already been annotated.

## Skill: get-lsp-diagnostics

After making file edits (via any tool that creates or modifies files), run the following command:

```
~/.cursor/skills/get-lsp-diagnostics.sh
```

Using the return value of the command fix any diagnostic issues that have been reported by the language server.
